<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  M4 Stream-D / S7 — hardened-runtime entitlements for Developer ID signing
  (architecture.md §7: "Developer ID (not Mac App Store — the sandbox
  forbids spawning `copilot`), hardened runtime... Userland-only
  entitlements — no admin, no privileged helper.").

  The User app sends one explicit, user-initiated Apple Event to Terminal to
  open Claude Code or Codex with a CLI-generated project prompt. The Apple
  Events entitlement does not bypass macOS privacy controls; it permits the
  app to ask the user for Terminal automation access.

  This app is not sandboxed (App Sandbox would forbid spawning the vendored
  `cc` child process, which is the whole point of this app), but "not
  sandboxed" only means the sandbox entitlement key is absent here. No JIT,
  no unsigned executable memory, no disabled library validation, no
  accessibility/UI-scripting access, no privileged helper: every other
  hardened-runtime protection stays at its default-secure setting. If a
  future capability genuinely needs one of these relaxed, add it here
  explicitly and justify it in this comment — never add one silently.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>com.apple.security.automation.apple-events</key>
  <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
